00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:29.689
It felt like such a natural thing
for them to build up to.

00:06:29.789 --> 00:06:33.393
But then the big debacle with Black Adam
in the Rock happened last year.

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:35.828
He had a huge falling out with DC,
where there was

00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:39.632
this big political power
play behind the scenes he wound up losing.

00:06:39.632 --> 00:06:43.403
James Gunn was hired as the new CEO,
the new Kevin Feige of DC Studios,

00:06:43.636 --> 00:06:44.771
and that was the end of it.

00:06:44.771 --> 00:06:48.841
Even though the Rock recently
was asked about all that drama.

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:51.010
And he actually took it like a champ.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:53.012
He's treating it
like water under the bridge now.

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:56.883
Like it doesn't bother him that much,
but it does sound like we will not see

00:06:56.883 --> 00:07:02.321
Black Adam versus Shazam in any kind of DC
movie for a long, a long time.

00:07:02.321 --> 00:07:04.390
And when they do
eventually do something like that,

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:06.726
the rock
will not be that version of Black. Adam.

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:11.130
So as much as being self-contained helps
the Shazam characters chances

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:15.001
of coming back in the future
and helped the movie avoid major Re edits

00:07:15.001 --> 00:07:18.571
after the fact, after James Gunn was hired
and they rebooted DC movies with this

00:07:18.571 --> 00:07:19.772
brand new plan,

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:23.176
is that it isn't quite as epic or earth
shattering is a film that you would

00:07:23.176 --> 00:07:26.913
normally expect is a sequel setting up
and paying off all these big things

00:07:26.913 --> 00:07:28.714
that they teased during the first movie.

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:30.049
There's still a lot of action
